## 8. Security Considerations

### 8.1 Authentication
- **API Credentials**: Use secure authentication from @file(config/credentials.yaml)
- **Token Handling**: Never log full tokens or secrets

### 8.2 Data Protection
- **Sensitive Content**: Truncate or hash sensitive memory content in logs
- **Personally Identifiable Information (PII)**: Mask or pseudonymize where appropriate
- **Log Protection**: Ensure logs are not world-readable

### 8.3 Access Control
- **Monitor Configuration**: Require admin privileges to modify settings
- **Log Access**: Restrict access to authorized users

